are many types of this like singly, doubly, and circular.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/d6fed00177b86520a05fdaa7b105d41e","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-22T05:42:56.386Z"},{"id":"XAVHeUSog","title":"How to scrape virtual scrolling with Puppeteer","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501789?url=https://filipvitas.medium.com/how-to-scrape-virtual-scrolling-with-puppeteer-f8b699e69b4c","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-scrape-virtual-scrolling-with-puppeteer-xavheusog","summary":"Virtual scrolling (windowing) is a technique where we don\u2019t display the entire content on the screen. Instead, we render what is in the view and a little bit on the top and bottom. This way we have a nice buffer of the content. On scrolling, a virtual scroller removes old content and adds new content into the view.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1dc651f99605697da72454ca008318a4","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-21T22:52:16.906Z"},{"id":"QTTYOWNYW","title":"Serverless JAMstack with NuxtJS, FaunaDB, GraphQL and Netlify","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501656?url=https://blog.bitsrc.io/bootstrapping-a-serverless-jamstack-with-nuxtjs-faunadb-graphql-and-netlify-905bdd3191f?gi=5428a8a56a77","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/serverless-jamstack-with-nuxtjs-faunadb-graphql-and-netlify-qttyownyw","summary":"Serverless JAMstack with NuxtJS, FaunaDB, GraphQL and Netlify. We will use Vue.js, TailwindCSS, Nuxt JS, FaunDB,GraphQL, and Paymon. The goal is to build a fully-equipped enterprise application using the JAM stack.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/b4a7646498b875c9e7ec270fb526b3c5","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-21T16:49:09.463Z"},{"id":"TW3oxZA--","title":"8 Different Places \u201cthis\u201d Can Point to in JavaScript","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501655?url=https://blog.bitsrc.io/where-exactly-does-this-point-to-in-javascript-2be1e3fad1fd?gi=9ad19aaa75d4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/8-different-places-this-can-point-to-in-javascript-tw3oxza","summary":"In ES5, this refers to the top-level object ( window in the browser) In strict mode, this behaves differently, as undefined. The first argument is undefined or null, which in non-strict mode points to window. In strict modes, it refers to a primitive value, which is a wrapped value and will not be an object.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/ac01a2ca8d25a30f56ec10c80e3b1ae3","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-21T15:34:18.203Z"},{"id":"H9XTMHyho","title":"Array.prototype.reduce's initial value is optional","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501417?url=https://www.stefanjudis.com/today-i-learned/the-array-prototype-reduces-initial-value-is-optional/","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/array-prototype-reduce-s-initial-value-is-optional-h9xtmhyho","summary":"reduce() is one of these underrated Array methods that can be tremendously useful to accumulate array items. Define an initial value, iterate over all array items and define a callback function to form a combined result. Each callback's return value is provided to the next entry callback so that you can sum numbers.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/827989151b2bfa0b07c5d7799dde802c","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-21T14:37:58.406Z"},{"id":"Z2egNVXTC","title":"You Can throw() Anything In JavaScript - And Other async/await Considerations","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501422?url=https://www.bennadel.com/blog/4210-you-can-throw-anything-in-javascript-and-other-async-await-considerations.htm","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/you-can-throw-anything-in-javascript---and-other-async-await-considerations-z2egnvxtc","summary":"You Can throw() Anything In JavaScript - And Other Async/await Considerations. Ben Nadel: Can you throw() anything in JavaScript? He shows how you can throw Promise objects in JavaScript. He also shows how to throw() an Error instead of an Error in an API call.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/2ffd6e06a02a74bec6ab6aa20350b69e","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-21T14:34:57.378Z"},{"id":"lfFyjMaH9","title":"What are wrapper objects for primitive values?","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501479?url=https://2ality.com/2022/02/wrapper-objects.html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-are-wrapper-objects-for-primitive-values--lffyjmah9","summary":"Each primitive type (except for the types of undefined and null ) has a corresponding wrapper class. The key purpose of these classes is to provide properties (mostly methods) for primitive values. wrapper classes can be function-called, which converts an arbitrary value to the primitive type that the class represents.","image":"https://javascriptkicks.com/img/favicon.png","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-21T14:33:31.083Z"},{"id":"ZdaVCTJxV","title":"4 Ways of Finding Elements in a JavaScript Array","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501713?url=https://javascript.plainenglish.io/4-ways-of-finding-elements-in-a-javascript-array-ba66cda8997?source=rss----4b3a1ed4f11c---4&gi=b4af20093ba8","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/4-ways-of-finding-elements-in-a-javascript-array-zdavctjxv","summary":"Arrays are the building blocks for data-based web apps. We can store and manipulate data using an Array easily. 4 Ways of Finding Elements in a JavaScript Array. 4 ways to find an element in an Array, along with some use cases explained with examples. Anshuman Bhardwaj.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3868b5047039bacc56c795bdfc07bb2b","num_upvotes":5,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2022-02-21T12:48:47.606Z"},{"id":"Q5AwYhOBQ","title":"How to Compare Objects in JavaScript","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501653?url=https://blog.bitsrc.io/how-to-compare-objects-in-javascript-f4eafef807fc?gi=e9e4c47b6ba7","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-to-compare-objects-in-javascript-q5awyhobq","summary":"How to Compare Objects in JavaScript. How to write a function that compares two objects and returns true if they are equal, and false if they're not. The function works for objects that contain simple, but not complex properties. The comparison operator (===) will return false because we can\u2019t directly compare 2 objects.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/deb9df261a374ad1a9bf9c8f1084fe56","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-21T11:26:06.176Z"},{"id":"Y_AnDFbx5","title":"Modern Test-Driven Development with TypeScript and Redux Slices","url":"https://javascriptkicks.com/r/501651?url=https://javascript.plainenglish.io/modern-test-driven-development-with-typescript-and-redux-slices-32c249fdc8fe?gi=6f8cac98ba4f","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/modern-test-driven-development-with-typescript-and-redux-slices-y-andfbx5","summary":"Unit testing is one of the most important but most neglected practises in Agile Software Development. TypeScript and Redux Slices make it easy to test your code in TypeScript/JavaScript. This article will show users of these tools how to unit test their code effectively.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/caa82ad4bc9eaea44eaa2d9e90a5c9c0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2022-02-21T09:18:12.905Z"}],"similar_handles":["electron","codemagic","geekflare","rubydispatch","implementing"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","hamelhusain","tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_"],"similar":[{"id":"electron","handle":"electron","name":"Electron","is_squad":false,"x":-5.6415,"y":2.6121,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":56,"image":"https://media.daily.d